From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:08:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Implement MSXML's extension functions in XPath and
 XSLT.

MSXML 4.0 and later have ms:utc, ms:number, ms:local-name,
ms:namespace-uri, ms:format-date, ms:format-time, ms:type-local-name,
ms:type-namespace-uri and ms:schema-info-available next to
ms:string-compare, in selectNodes() and in XSLT alike.  Wine had only
ms:string-compare, in XPath.  msxsl.c answers them as Windows 11 does,
and both the XPath engine and libxslt (registered per transformation
when the source is MSXML 4.0 or later) call it:

- ms:utc() reads an XML Schema date, time, dateTime or g* value, moves
  it to UTC and writes it without the zone, with dashes for the parts it
  lacks (----------T10:00:00) and milliseconds rounded to three digits;
- ms:number() reads an XML Schema double (1e3, INF, NaN);
- ms:format-date() and ms:format-time() format through GetDateFormat()
  and GetTimeFormat(), in UTC, with the language's own format by default;
- ms:namespace-uri() resolves the prefix on the node, not on the
  stylesheet or SelectionNamespaces.

A language argument is taken only when Rfc1766ToLcidW() answers S_OK
for it, so de and en-us are languages and de-DE is not.  A
transformation that such an argument stops now fails with E_FAIL
instead of returning an empty string.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

